IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lga-time`

-- Legislation Act 2003 (Commonwealth), Chapter 2 Part 2: compilations (sections 15P to 15X).
-- Text: C2004A01224.txt, compilation C2019C00084; it is not the authorised text.
-- Same conventions as lga-register.l4: JUST TRUE (the text says yes), JUST FALSE (the text says no), NOTHING (the text does not say).
-- The 28 days of sections 15R(3) and 15T(2) are counted by lga-time.l4.

§ `Section 15P: information in a registered compilation`

DECLARE `Facts about a registered compilation` HAS
    `it includes the compilation date`                                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `editorial changes were made in preparing it`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `it includes a statement that editorial changes have been made and a brief outline of the changes`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `it includes details (including commencement details) of any Act or instrument that amends the principal law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it includes the amendment history of provisions of the principal law`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `it includes any further information prescribed by the rules`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the First Parliamentary Counsel is satisfied that the details of amending laws are otherwise appropriately available on an approved website` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the First Parliamentary Counsel is satisfied that the amendment history is otherwise appropriately available on an approved website`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the First Parliamentary Counsel is satisfied that the further prescribed information is otherwise appropriately available on an approved website` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the compilation indicates in general terms how users of the Register may access that information on the approved website` IS A BOOLEAN

-- jural: claim of nobody the text names | duty of whoever prepares the registered compilation (the text does not say who)
-- Where the rules prescribe no further information, the field "it includes any further information prescribed by the rules" holds trivially: it is TRUE.
-- Paragraphs (c) to (e) may be left out of the compilation if the conditions of subsection (2) are met for that paragraph.
-- src:475 | (1) Without limiting the information that a registered compilation of an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument (the principal law) may include, the registered compilation must include the following information:
-- src:476 | (a) the compilation date;
-- src:477 | (b) if any editorial changes are made in preparing the compilation—a statement that editorial changes have been made and a brief outline of the changes in general terms;
-- src:478 | (c) details (including commencement details) of any Act or instrument that amends the principal law;
-- src:479 | (d) the amendment history of provisions of the principal law;
-- src:480 | (e) any further information prescribed by the rules.
-- src:481 | (2) However, the information mentioned in any of paragraphs (1)(c) to (e) does not need to be included in the compilation if:
-- src:482 | (a) the First Parliamentary Counsel is satisfied that the information mentioned in that paragraph is otherwise appropriately available on an approved website to users of the Federal Register of Legislation; and
-- src:483 | (b) the compilation indicates in general terms how users of the Register may access that information on the approved website.
@ref s 15P(1) and (2) (src:475-483)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts about a registered compilation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15P: the registered compilation includes the information it must include` MEANS
        `the facts`'s `it includes the compilation date`
    AND (`the facts`'s `editorial changes were made in preparing it` IMPLIES `the facts`'s `it includes a statement that editorial changes have been made and a brief outline of the changes`)
    AND (   `the facts`'s `it includes details (including commencement details) of any Act or instrument that amends the principal law`
         OR (    `the facts`'s `the First Parliamentary Counsel is satisfied that the details of amending laws are otherwise appropriately available on an approved website`
             AND `the facts`'s `the compilation indicates in general terms how users of the Register may access that information on the approved website`))
    AND (   `the facts`'s `it includes the amendment history of provisions of the principal law`
         OR (    `the facts`'s `the First Parliamentary Counsel is satisfied that the amendment history is otherwise appropriately available on an approved website`
             AND `the facts`'s `the compilation indicates in general terms how users of the Register may access that information on the approved website`))
    AND (   `the facts`'s `it includes any further information prescribed by the rules`
         OR (    `the facts`'s `the First Parliamentary Counsel is satisfied that the further prescribed information is otherwise appropriately available on an approved website`
             AND `the facts`'s `the compilation indicates in general terms how users of the Register may access that information on the approved website`))

§ `Section 15Q: required and discretionary compilation events`

DECLARE `Facts about an event for section 15Q(1)` HAS
    `the Act or instrument is expressly amended`                                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amendment is made under section 48C or 48D`                                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the instrument is a disallowable legislative instrument`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `a provision of the instrument is disallowed under section 42`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `a provision of another disallowable legislative instrument has amended a provision of the instrument, but the amending instrument or provision is disallowed under section 42` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a provision of the Act or instrument is repealed under another Act or instrument (other than this Act), or because of the making of another Act or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
    `something else happens that is prescribed by the rules for the purposes of paragraph (1)(d)`                      IS A BOOLEAN

-- "occurs ... when": a "when" list answers JUST FALSE for an event that matches none of its paragraphs.
-- src:486 | (1) A required compilation event occurs for an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument when:
-- src:487 | (a) the Act or instrument is expressly amended (otherwise than under section 48C or 48D); or
-- src:488 | (b) in the case of a disallowable legislative instrument:
-- src:489 | (i) a provision of the instrument is disallowed under section 42; or
-- src:490 | (ii) a provision of another disallowable legislative instrument has amended a provision of the instrument, but the amending instrument, or the amending provision, is disallowed under section 42; or
-- src:491 | (c) a provision of the Act or instrument is repealed under another Act or instrument (other than this Act), or because of the making of another Act or instrument; or
-- src:492 | (d) something else happens that is prescribed by the rules for the purposes of this paragraph.
@ref s 15Q(1) (src:486-492)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts about an event for section 15Q(1)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15Q(1): a required compilation event occurs` MEANS
    IF    (`the facts`'s `the Act or instrument is expressly amended` AND NOT `the facts`'s `the amendment is made under section 48C or 48D`)
       OR (`the facts`'s `the instrument is a disallowable legislative instrument`
           AND (`the facts`'s `a provision of the instrument is disallowed under section 42`
                OR `the facts`'s `a provision of another disallowable legislative instrument has amended a provision of the instrument, but the amending instrument or provision is disallowed under section 42`))
       OR `the facts`'s `a provision of the Act or instrument is repealed under another Act or instrument (other than this Act), or because of the making of another Act or instrument`
       OR `the facts`'s `something else happens that is prescribed by the rules for the purposes of paragraph (1)(d)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `Facts about an event for section 15Q(2)` HAS
    `a provision of the Act or instrument commences`                                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument amended by section 48C or 48D`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Act or instrument is modified`                                                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Act or instrument is impliedly amended`                                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `a provision of the Act or instrument is repealed under another provision of that Act or instrument`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `no compilation has been registered and the text as registered otherwise ceases to show the text of the Act or instrument as in force` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a compilation has been registered and the text of the latest registered compilation otherwise ceases to show the text of the Act or instrument as amended (if at all) and in force` IS A BOOLEAN
    `something else happens that is prescribed by the rules for the purposes of paragraph (2)(h)`                     IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:493 | (2) A discretionary compilation event occurs for an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument when:
-- src:494 | (a) a provision of the Act or instrument commences; or
-- src:495 | (b) in the case of a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument—the instrument is amended by section 48C or 48D; or
-- src:496 | (c) the Act or instrument is modified; or
-- src:497 | (d) the Act or instrument is impliedly amended; or
-- src:498 | (e) a provision of the Act or instrument is repealed under another provision of that Act or instrument; or
-- src:499 | (f) if no compilation has been registered for the Act or instrument—the text of the Act or instrument as registered otherwise ceases to show the text of the Act or instrument as in force; or
-- src:500 | (g) if a compilation has been registered for the Act or instrument—the text of the latest registered compilation otherwise ceases to show the text of the Act or instrument as amended (if at all) and in force; or
-- src:501 | (h) something else happens that is prescribed by the rules for the purposes of this paragraph.
-- src:502 | Note: Sections 48C and 48D provide for the automatic repeal of amending, repealing and commencement provisions of legislative instruments and notifiable instruments.
@ref s 15Q(2) (src:493-502)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts about an event for section 15Q(2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15Q(2): a discretionary compilation event occurs` MEANS
    IF    `the facts`'s `a provision of the Act or instrument commences`
       OR `the facts`'s `it is a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument amended by section 48C or 48D`
       OR `the facts`'s `the Act or instrument is modified`
       OR `the facts`'s `the Act or instrument is impliedly amended`
       OR `the facts`'s `a provision of the Act or instrument is repealed under another provision of that Act or instrument`
       OR `the facts`'s `no compilation has been registered and the text as registered otherwise ceases to show the text of the Act or instrument as in force`
       OR `the facts`'s `a compilation has been registered and the text of the latest registered compilation otherwise ceases to show the text of the Act or instrument as amended (if at all) and in force`
       OR `the facts`'s `something else happens that is prescribed by the rules for the purposes of paragraph (2)(h)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:504 | (3) For the purposes of this Division, an Act or instrument is (subject to subsection (4)) amended by an Act or instrument, or a provision of an Act or instrument, when the amending Act or provision commences.
@ref s 15Q(3) (src:504-504)
GIVEN `the amending Act or provision has commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15Q(3): the Act or instrument is amended by the amending Act or provision` MEANS
    IF `the amending Act or provision has commenced` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- jural: privilege of the rule-maker and the First Parliamentary Counsel | no-right of anyone to require a compilation for a retrospective commencement
-- Subsection (4) has two sentences: no duty to compile for a retrospective commencement; but a compilation may be prepared and lodged.
-- src:505 | (4) Despite any other provision of this Act, a compilation of an Act or instrument is not required to be prepared or lodged for registration to take account of a retrospective commencement of an amendment of the Act or instrument. However, such a compilation of an Act or instrument may be prepared and lodged for registration.
@ref s 15Q(4) (src:505-505)
GIVEN `the amendment commences retrospectively` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15Q(4): a compilation is required to be prepared or lodged for registration to take account of the retrospective commencement` MEANS
    IF `the amendment commences retrospectively` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 15Q(4) (src:505-505)
GIVEN `the amendment commences retrospectively` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15Q(4): a compilation may be prepared and lodged for registration to take account of the retrospective commencement` MEANS
    IF `the amendment commences retrospectively` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 15R and 15S: lodging a compilation of an instrument`

-- Section 15R does not apply to what the rules prescribe (subsection (4)); the rules are not among the sources, so whether they do is an input.
-- jural: claim of the First Parliamentary Counsel | duty of the rule-maker
-- src:508 | (1) If a required compilation event occurs for a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, the rule-maker must prepare and lodge for registration a compilation of the instrument for registration.
-- src:509 | Compilation date
-- src:510 | (2) The compilation date for the compilation must be the date of the required compilation event.
@ref s 15R(1) and (2) (src:508-510)
GIVEN `a required compilation event occurs for the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rules prescribe that section 15R does not apply to this instrument, or in these circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15R(1): the rule-maker must prepare and lodge a compilation of the instrument for registration` MEANS
    IF `the rules prescribe that section 15R does not apply to this instrument, or in these circumstances`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE (IF `a required compilation event occurs for the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)

@ref s 15R(2) (src:510-510)
GIVEN `a required compilation event occurs for the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the required compilation event` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 15R(2): the compilation date for the compilation` MEANS
    IF `a required compilation event occurs for the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` THEN JUST `the date of the required compilation event` ELSE NOTHING

-- jural: claim of the First Parliamentary Counsel | duty of the rule-maker
-- The period is "within 28 days after the event occurs, or a longer period allowed by the First Parliamentary Counsel".
-- src:512 | (3) The rule-maker must lodge for registration the compilation required by subsection (1) within 28 days after the event occurs, or a longer period allowed by the First Parliamentary Counsel.
@ref s 15R(3) (src:512-512)
GIVEN `the day the event occurs` IS A DATE
      `the day the compilation is lodged` IS A DATE
      `the First Parliamentary Counsel has allowed a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the longer period allowed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15R(3): the compilation is lodged in time` MEANS
    `the day the compilation is lodged` AT MOST
        (IF `the First Parliamentary Counsel has allowed a longer period`
         THEN `the later of two days` (`s 15R(3): the last day for lodging a compilation after a required compilation event` `the day the event occurs`) `the last day of the longer period allowed`
         ELSE `s 15R(3): the last day for lodging a compilation after a required compilation event` `the day the event occurs`)

-- src:514 | (4) This section does not apply to legislative instruments or notifiable instruments, or in circumstances, prescribed by rules made for the purposes of this subsection.
-- src:515 | Example: A circumstance prescribed by the rules may be if the First Parliamentary Counsel prepares and registers a compilation of a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument.
@ref s 15R(4) (src:514-515)
GIVEN `the rules prescribe that section 15R does not apply to this instrument, or in these circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15R(4): section 15R applies` MEANS
    IF `the rules prescribe that section 15R does not apply to this instrument, or in these circumstances` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- jural: power of the First Parliamentary Counsel | liability of the rule-maker
-- src:518 | (1) If a discretionary compilation event occurs for a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, the First Parliamentary Counsel may, by written notice given to the rule-maker, require the rule-maker, within a period stated in the notice, to prepare and lodge for registration a compilation of the instrument for registration.
@ref s 15S(1) (src:518-518)
GIVEN `a discretionary compilation event occurs for the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15S(1): the First Parliamentary Counsel may by written notice require the rule-maker to prepare and lodge a compilation within the period stated` MEANS
    IF `a discretionary compilation event occurs for the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- jural: claim of the First Parliamentary Counsel | duty of the rule-maker
-- src:520 | (2) The compilation date for the compilation must be the date of the discretionary compilation event.
@ref s 15S(2) (src:520-520)
GIVEN `a discretionary compilation event occurs for the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the discretionary compilation event` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 15S(2): the compilation date for the compilation` MEANS
    IF `a discretionary compilation event occurs for the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` THEN JUST `the date of the discretionary compilation event` ELSE NOTHING

-- jural: claim of the First Parliamentary Counsel | duty of the rule-maker
-- src:522 | (3) If a notice is given under subsection (1) to a rule-maker for an instrument, the rule-maker must lodge for registration a compilation of the instrument within the period stated in the notice, or a longer period allowed by the First Parliamentary Counsel.
@ref s 15S(3) (src:522-522)
GIVEN `a notice is given under subsection (1) to the rule-maker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the compilation is lodged` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period stated in the notice, or of a longer period allowed by the First Parliamentary Counsel` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15S(3): the compilation is lodged within the period` MEANS
    IF `a notice is given under subsection (1) to the rule-maker`
    THEN JUST (`the day the compilation is lodged` AT MOST `the last day of the period stated in the notice, or of a longer period allowed by the First Parliamentary Counsel`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 15T: registering a compilation`

-- jural: claim of nobody the text names | duty of the First Parliamentary Counsel
-- src:525 | (1) If a required compilation event occurs for an Act, the First Parliamentary Counsel must prepare and register a compilation of the Act as soon as practicable afterwards.
@ref s 15T(1) (src:525-525)
GIVEN `a required compilation event occurs for an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15T(1): the First Parliamentary Counsel must prepare and register a compilation of the Act as soon as practicable afterwards` MEANS
    IF `a required compilation event occurs for an Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- jural: claim of nobody the text names | duty of the First Parliamentary Counsel
-- src:527 | (2) If a required compilation event occurs for a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, the First Parliamentary Counsel must register a compilation of the instrument:
-- src:528 | (a) if a compilation is lodged for registration within 28 days after the event, or within a longer period allowed by the First Parliamentary Counsel—as soon as practicable after lodgement; or
-- src:529 | (b) if a compilation is not lodged for registration within that period—as soon as practicable after the end of the period.
@ref s 15T(2) (src:527-529)
GIVEN `a required compilation event occurs for the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15T(2): the First Parliamentary Counsel must register a compilation of the instrument` MEANS
    IF `a required compilation event occurs for the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- The point after which the Counsel must register "as soon as practicable": the lodgement day if lodged within the period (paragraph (a)), otherwise the end of the period (paragraph (b)).
@ref s 15T(2)(a) and (b) (src:527-529)
GIVEN `the day the event occurs` IS A DATE
      `the compilation is lodged within 28 days after the event, or within a longer period allowed by the First Parliamentary Counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the compilation is lodged` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the longer period allowed` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 15T(2): the day after which the First Parliamentary Counsel must register as soon as practicable` MEANS
    IF `the compilation is lodged within 28 days after the event, or within a longer period allowed by the First Parliamentary Counsel`
    THEN `the day the compilation is lodged`
    ELSE
        CONSIDER `the last day of the longer period allowed`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 15T(2)(a): the last day of the 28 days after a required compilation event` `the day the event occurs`
        WHEN JUST d THEN `the later of two days` (`s 15T(2)(a): the last day of the 28 days after a required compilation event` `the day the event occurs`) d

-- jural: claim of nobody the text names | duty of the First Parliamentary Counsel
-- src:530 | (3) However, if a required compilation event occurs for a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, and section 15R does not apply because of subsection 15R(4), the First Parliamentary Counsel must prepare and register a compilation of the instrument as soon as practicable afterwards.
@ref s 15T(3) (src:530-530)
GIVEN `a required compilation event occurs for the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 15R does not apply because of subsection 15R(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15T(3): the First Parliamentary Counsel must prepare and register a compilation of the instrument as soon as practicable afterwards` MEANS
    IF `a required compilation event occurs for the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` AND `section 15R does not apply because of subsection 15R(4)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- Subsection (6) says the Counsel may compile even if neither kind of event has occurred, so the "if" of subsection (4) is not read as "only if": the answer when no event occurred is NOTHING, not JUST FALSE.
-- jural: privilege of the First Parliamentary Counsel | no-right of users of the Register
-- src:532 | (4) If a discretionary compilation event occurs for an Act or a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, the First Parliamentary Counsel may prepare and register a compilation of the Act or instrument.
@ref s 15T(4) (src:532-532)
GIVEN `a discretionary compilation event occurs for the Act or legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15T(4): the First Parliamentary Counsel may prepare and register a compilation of the Act or instrument` MEANS
    IF `a discretionary compilation event occurs for the Act or legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- jural: claim of nobody the text names | duty of the First Parliamentary Counsel
-- src:533 | (5) If a discretionary compilation event occurs for a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, and the First Parliamentary Counsel gives the rule-maker for the instrument a notice under section 15S, the First Parliamentary Counsel must register a compilation of the instrument:
-- src:534 | (a) if a compilation is lodged for registration within the period stated in the notice, or within a longer period allowed by the First Parliamentary Counsel—as soon as practicable after lodgement; or
-- src:535 | (b) if a compilation is not lodged for registration within that period—as soon as practicable after the end of the period.
@ref s 15T(5) (src:533-535)
GIVEN `a discretionary compilation event occurs for the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the First Parliamentary Counsel has given the rule-maker a notice under section 15S` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15T(5): the First Parliamentary Counsel must register a compilation of the instrument` MEANS
    IF `a discretionary compilation event occurs for the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` AND `the First Parliamentary Counsel has given the rule-maker a notice under section 15S` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- jural: privilege of the First Parliamentary Counsel | no-right of users of the Register
-- src:537 | (6) The First Parliamentary Counsel may prepare and register a compilation of an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument even if neither a required compilation event nor a discretionary compilation event has occurred for the Act or instrument.
@ref s 15T(6) (src:537-537)
GIVEN `it is an Act, a legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15T(6): the First Parliamentary Counsel may prepare and register a compilation even if neither kind of compilation event has occurred` MEANS
    IF `it is an Act, a legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- jural: claim of nobody the text names | duty of the First Parliamentary Counsel
-- src:539 | (7) The First Parliamentary Counsel must ensure that a registered compilation of an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument is no longer shown on the Register as a compilation currently in force as soon as practicable after:
-- src:540 | (a) the Act or instrument is repealed; or
-- src:541 | (b) for a disallowable legislative instrument—the instrument is disallowed under section 42.
@ref s 15T(7) (src:539-541)
GIVEN `the Act or instrument is repealed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a disallowable legislative instrument that is disallowed under section 42` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15T(7): the First Parliamentary Counsel must ensure that the registered compilation is no longer shown on the Register as a compilation currently in force` MEANS
    IF `the Act or instrument is repealed` OR `it is a disallowable legislative instrument that is disallowed under section 42` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 15V and 15W: editorial changes and other changes`

-- Subsection (2) says "only if": a change not considered desirable for (a) or (b) answers JUST FALSE.
-- jural: power of the First Parliamentary Counsel | liability of anyone whose rights the changed text governs
-- src:561 | (1) In preparing a compilation of an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument for registration (including a compilation that has been lodged for registration), the First Parliamentary Counsel may make editorial changes to any text that is part of the Act or instrument.
-- src:562 | Note 1: For what is an editorial change, see section 15X.
-- src:563 | Note 2: For what text forms part of the Act or instrument, see section 13 of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 (which applies in relation to instruments under section 13 of this Act).
-- src:564 | (2) The First Parliamentary Counsel may make an editorial change to an Act or instrument under subsection (1) only if he or she considers the change to be desirable to:
-- src:565 | (a) bring the Act or instrument into line, or more closely into line, with legislative drafting practice being used by the Office of Parliamentary Counsel; or
-- src:566 | (b) correct an error, or ensure that a misdescribed amendment of the Act or instrument is given effect to as intended.
@ref s 15V(1) and (2) (src:561-566)
GIVEN `the change is made in preparing a compilation for registration (including a compilation that has been lodged for registration)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the text is part of the Act or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the First Parliamentary Counsel considers the change desirable to bring the Act or instrument into line with legislative drafting practice used by the Office of Parliamentary Counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the First Parliamentary Counsel considers the change desirable to correct an error, or to ensure that a misdescribed amendment is given effect to as intended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15V(1) and (2): the First Parliamentary Counsel may make the editorial change` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the change is made in preparing a compilation for registration (including a compilation that has been lodged for registration)` AND `the text is part of the Act or instrument`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE
        IF `the First Parliamentary Counsel considers the change desirable to bring the Act or instrument into line with legislative drafting practice used by the Office of Parliamentary Counsel`
           OR `the First Parliamentary Counsel considers the change desirable to correct an error, or to ensure that a misdescribed amendment is given effect to as intended`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- jural: power of the First Parliamentary Counsel | liability of anyone whose rights the changed text governs
-- src:568 | (3) In preparing a compilation of an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument for registration (including a compilation that has been lodged for registration), the First Parliamentary Counsel may make changes to the Act or instrument that affect the format, layout or printing style of the Act or instrument, or any other presentational aspect of the Act or instrument.
-- src:569 | (4) The First Parliamentary Counsel may make a change to an Act or instrument under subsection (3) only if he or she considers the change to be desirable to bring the Act or instrument into line, or more closely into line, with legislative drafting practice being used by the Office of Parliamentary Counsel.
@ref s 15V(3) and (4) (src:568-569)
GIVEN `the change is made in preparing a compilation for registration (including a compilation that has been lodged for registration)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change affects the format, layout or printing style of the Act or instrument, or another presentational aspect of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the First Parliamentary Counsel considers the change desirable to bring the Act or instrument into line with legislative drafting practice used by the Office of Parliamentary Counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15V(3) and (4): the First Parliamentary Counsel may make the presentational change` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the change is made in preparing a compilation for registration (including a compilation that has been lodged for registration)` AND `the change affects the format, layout or printing style of the Act or instrument, or another presentational aspect of it`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE
        IF `the First Parliamentary Counsel considers the change desirable to bring the Act or instrument into line with legislative drafting practice used by the Office of Parliamentary Counsel`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- jural: power of the First Parliamentary Counsel | liability of anyone whose rights the changed text governs
-- src:571 | (5) In preparing a compilation of an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument (including a compilation that has been lodged for registration), the First Parliamentary Counsel may include, omit or change any text that is not part of the Act or instrument, including (without limitation) any of the following:
-- src:572 | (a) a table of contents or other provision that only describes the arrangement of the Act or instrument (or provisions of the Act or instrument) into groups of provisions;
-- src:573 | (b) a reader’s guide, simplified outline or similar text that only describes the nature or effect of the Act or instrument;
-- src:574 | (c) text, known as alternative text (or “alt text”), that does not form part of the Act or instrument because of subsection 13(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 (including that subsection as applied by section 13 of this Act);
-- src:575 | (d) for an instrument—instrument-making words.
-- src:576 | Note: For paragraph (c), alternative text may, for example, aurally indicate the effect of a graphic image in an Act or instrument to assist users of an approved website who have visual disabilities.
@ref s 15V(5) (src:571-576)
GIVEN `the change is made in preparing a compilation (including a compilation that has been lodged for registration)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the text is not part of the Act or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15V(5): the First Parliamentary Counsel may include, omit or change the text` MEANS
    IF `the change is made in preparing a compilation (including a compilation that has been lodged for registration)` AND `the text is not part of the Act or instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- jural: immunity of anyone bound by the Act or instrument | disability of the First Parliamentary Counsel
-- src:578 | (6) The First Parliamentary Counsel must not make a change to an Act or instrument under this section that would change the effect of the Act or instrument.
-- src:579 | (7) Subsection (6) does not prevent the First Parliamentary Counsel making a change to an Act or instrument mentioned in paragraph (2)(m) of the definition of editorial change in subsection 15X(2), or any editorial change consequential on such a change, as mentioned in paragraph (2)(q) of that definition.
-- src:580 | Note: Such a change consists of the incorporation into an Act or instrument of an application, savings, transitional, validation or similar provision that is contained in an amending Act or instrument.
@ref s 15V(6) and (7) (src:578-580)
GIVEN `the change would change the effect of the Act or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a change mentioned in paragraph (2)(m) of the definition of editorial change in subsection 15X(2), or an editorial change consequential on such a change as mentioned in paragraph (2)(q)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15V(6): the First Parliamentary Counsel must not make the change` MEANS
    IF `it is a change mentioned in paragraph (2)(m) of the definition of editorial change in subsection 15X(2), or an editorial change consequential on such a change as mentioned in paragraph (2)(q)`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE (IF `the change would change the effect of the Act or instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)

-- src:582 | If the First Parliamentary Counsel makes an editorial change to an Act or instrument under section 15V in preparing a compilation, then, after the registration of the compilation:
-- src:583 | (a) the Act or instrument has effect for all purposes as if the change had been made by an amendment of the Act or instrument that commenced on the day the compilation was registered; and
-- src:584 | (b) the Act or instrument may be further amended as if the change had been made by an amendment of the Act or instrument.
@ref s 15W (src:582-584)
GIVEN `the First Parliamentary Counsel makes an editorial change to the Act or instrument under section 15V in preparing a compilation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the compilation has been registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15W(a): the Act or instrument has effect as if the change had been made by an amendment that commenced on the day the compilation was registered` MEANS
    IF `the First Parliamentary Counsel makes an editorial change to the Act or instrument under section 15V in preparing a compilation` AND `the compilation has been registered` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref s 15W(b) (src:584-584)
GIVEN `the First Parliamentary Counsel makes an editorial change to the Act or instrument under section 15V in preparing a compilation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the compilation has been registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15W(b): the Act or instrument may be further amended as if the change had been made by an amendment` MEANS
    IF `the First Parliamentary Counsel makes an editorial change to the Act or instrument under section 15V in preparing a compilation` AND `the compilation has been registered` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§ `Section 15X: what an editorial change is`

DECLARE `Change for section 15X(2)` IS ONE OF
    `15X(2)(a): goes only to a matter of spelling, punctuation, grammar or syntax, or the use of conjunctives and disjunctives`
    `15X(2)(b)(i): updates a reference to a law covered by subsection (3), or to a provision of such a law`
    `15X(2)(b)(ii): updates a reference to a person, body or other entity, or an office, position, place, document or thing`
    `15X(2)(c): changes the short title of an Act, the name of an instrument, or the name of the types of provision in an instrument`
    `15X(2)(d): numbers or renumbers a provision`
    `15X(2)(e): changes the order of definitions or other provisions`
    `15X(2)(f): replaces a reference to a provision of a law covered by subsection (3) with a different form of reference`
    `15X(2)(g): changes the way of referring to or expressing a number, year, date, time, amount of money or other amount, penalty, quantity, measurement or other matter, idea or concept`
    `15X(2)(h): changes language that indicates gender or that could be taken to indicate gender`
    `15X(2)(i): omits or changes a table of contents or other provision that only describes the arrangement of the provisions into groups`
    `15X(2)(j): omits or changes a reader's guide, simplified outline or other text that only describes the nature or effect of the Act or instrument`
    `15X(2)(k): omits a provision, or a reference to a law covered by subsection (3), that has expired, is exhausted or spent, or is otherwise obsolete or redundant`
    `15X(2)(l): omits, inserts or changes a term that identifies a provision as a provision, or part of a provision`
    `15X(2)(m): incorporates into the principal law an application, savings, transitional, validation or similar provision contained in another Act or instrument that amends it`
    `15X(2)(n): shows the effect of an amendment, or is consequential on it`
    `15X(2)(o): gives effect as intended to a misdescribed amendment`
    `15X(2)(p): corrects an error covered by subsection (4)`
    `15X(2)(q): is consequential on any other editorial change`
    `any other change`

-- "An editorial change ... is a change made by the First Parliamentary Counsel that: (a) ... or (q)": a definition, so a change that matches no paragraph is JUST FALSE.
-- src:588 | (2) An editorial change to an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument is a change made by the First Parliamentary Counsel that:
-- src:589 | (a) goes only to a matter of spelling, punctuation, grammar or syntax, or the use of conjunctives and disjunctives; or
-- src:590 | (b) updates a reference to:
-- src:591 | (i) a law covered by subsection (3) (or a provision of such a law); or
-- src:592 | (ii) a person, body or other entity, or an office, position, place, document or thing; or
-- src:593 | (c) changes the short title of an Act or the name of an instrument, or the name of the types of provision in an instrument; or
-- src:594 | (d) numbers or renumbers a provision of the Act or instrument; or
-- src:595 | (e) changes the order of definitions or other provisions of the Act or instrument; or
-- src:596 | (f) replaces a reference to a provision of a law covered by subsection (3) with a different form of reference to the provision; or
-- src:597 | (g) changes the way of referring to or expressing a number, year, date, time, amount of money or other amount, penalty, quantity, measurement or other matter, idea or concept; or
-- src:598 | Example: A reference in a form to “this [blank] day of [blank] 19…” may be changed to “[Date]”.
-- src:599 | (h) changes language that indicates gender or that could be taken to indicate gender; or
-- src:600 | (i) omits or changes a table of contents or other provision that only describes the arrangement of the Act or instrument (or provisions of the Act or instrument) into groups of provisions; or
-- src:601 | (j) omits or changes a reader’s guide, simplified outline or other text that only describes the nature or effect of the Act or instrument; or
-- src:602 | (k) omits a provision, or a reference to a law covered by subsection (3) (or a provision of such a law) that has expired, the operation of which is exhausted or spent, or that is otherwise obsolete or redundant; or
-- src:603 | (l) omits, inserts or changes a term that identifies a provision of the Act or instrument as a provision, or part of a provision, of the Act or instrument; or
-- src:604 | Examples: The following are examples of references to provisions:
-- src:605 | (a) of these regulations;
-- src:606 | (b) of this regulation;
-- src:607 | (c) of this section;
-- src:608 | (d) hereof;
-- src:609 | (e) said.
-- src:610 | (m) incorporates into the Act or instrument (the principal law) an application, savings, transitional, validation or similar provision that is contained in another Act or instrument that amends the principal law; or
-- src:611 | (n) shows the effect of any amendment of the Act or instrument, or is consequential on any such amendment; or
-- src:612 | Example: The heading to a section may be changed to reflect the effect of an amendment of the section.
-- src:613 | (o) if an amendment of the Act or instrument is misdescribed by an amending Act or instrument—gives effect to the misdescribed amendment as intended; or
-- src:614 | (p) corrects an error covered by subsection (4); or
-- src:615 | (q) is consequential on any other editorial change made to the Act or instrument or to another Act or instrument.
@ref s 15X(2) (src:588-615)
GIVEN `the change is made by the First Parliamentary Counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change` IS A `Change for section 15X(2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15X(2): the change is an editorial change` MEANS
    IF NOT `the change is made by the First Parliamentary Counsel` THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE
        CONSIDER `the change`
        WHEN `any other change` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `15X(2)(a): goes only to a matter of spelling, punctuation, grammar or syntax, or the use of conjunctives and disjunctives` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `15X(2)(b)(i): updates a reference to a law covered by subsection (3), or to a provision of such a law` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `15X(2)(b)(ii): updates a reference to a person, body or other entity, or an office, position, place, document or thing` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `15X(2)(c): changes the short title of an Act, the name of an instrument, or the name of the types of provision in an instrument` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `15X(2)(d): numbers or renumbers a provision` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `15X(2)(e): changes the order of definitions or other provisions` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `15X(2)(f): replaces a reference to a provision of a law covered by subsection (3) with a different form of reference` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `15X(2)(g): changes the way of referring to or expressing a number, year, date, time, amount of money or other amount, penalty, quantity, measurement or other matter, idea or concept` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `15X(2)(h): changes language that indicates gender or that could be taken to indicate gender` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `15X(2)(i): omits or changes a table of contents or other provision that only describes the arrangement of the provisions into groups` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `15X(2)(j): omits or changes a reader's guide, simplified outline or other text that only describes the nature or effect of the Act or instrument` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `15X(2)(k): omits a provision, or a reference to a law covered by subsection (3), that has expired, is exhausted or spent, or is otherwise obsolete or redundant` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `15X(2)(l): omits, inserts or changes a term that identifies a provision as a provision, or part of a provision` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `15X(2)(m): incorporates into the principal law an application, savings, transitional, validation or similar provision contained in another Act or instrument that amends it` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `15X(2)(n): shows the effect of an amendment, or is consequential on it` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `15X(2)(o): gives effect as intended to a misdescribed amendment` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `15X(2)(p): corrects an error covered by subsection (4)` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `15X(2)(q): is consequential on any other editorial change` THEN JUST TRUE

-- src:616 | (3) This subsection covers the following laws:
-- src:617 | (a) an Act;
-- src:618 | (b) an instrument made under an Act or another power given by law;
-- src:619 | (c) an Act of a State, a Territory or New Zealand, or an instrument made under such an Act.
@ref s 15X(3) (src:616-619)
GIVEN `it is an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an instrument made under an Act or another power given by law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an Act of a State, a Territory or New Zealand, or an instrument made under such an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15X(3): the law is covered by this subsection` MEANS
    IF `it is an Act` OR `it is an instrument made under an Act or another power given by law` OR `it is an Act of a State, a Territory or New Zealand, or an instrument made under such an Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Error for section 15X(4)` IS ONE OF
    `typographical and clerical errors`
    `grammatical and spelling errors, and errors of punctuation`
    `errors in numbering, cross-referencing and alphabetical ordering`
    `errors in references to laws or instruments, or provisions of such laws, covered by subsection (3)`
    `errors in or arising out of an amendment of an Act or instrument`
    `any other error of a nature similar to those in paragraphs (a) to (e)`
    `any other error for section 15X(4)`

-- "This subsection covers the following errors": an unclosed list, so an error outside it is NOTHING.
-- src:620 | (4) This subsection covers the following errors:
-- src:621 | (a) typographical and clerical errors;
-- src:622 | (b) grammatical and spelling errors, and errors of punctuation;
-- src:623 | (c) errors in numbering, cross-referencing and alphabetical ordering;
-- src:624 | (d) errors in references to laws or instruments, or provisions of such laws, covered by subsection (3);
-- src:625 | (e) errors in or arising out of an amendment of an Act or instrument, including errors relating to the number of times such an amendment is expressed to be made;
-- src:626 | (f) any other errors of a nature similar to those mentioned in paragraphs (a) to (e).
@ref s 15X(4) (src:620-626)
GIVEN `the error` IS AN `Error for section 15X(4)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15X(4): the error is covered by this subsection` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the error`
    WHEN `any other error for section 15X(4)` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `typographical and clerical errors` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `grammatical and spelling errors, and errors of punctuation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `errors in numbering, cross-referencing and alphabetical ordering` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `errors in references to laws or instruments, or provisions of such laws, covered by subsection (3)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `errors in or arising out of an amendment of an Act or instrument` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `any other error of a nature similar to those in paragraphs (a) to (e)` THEN JUST TRUE
